    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d137">

                <pb facs="0222" n="120" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg120"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 14911/21–22.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chinese
                        Minister.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-11-27"><hi rendition="#italic">November 27,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 25th instant, with which was inclosed a translation of an
                    imperial message addressed to the President in acknowledgment of the message of
                    condolence from the President upon the demise of Their Imperial Majesties, the
                    Emperor and the Empress Dowager of China.</p>
                <p>The translation of the imperial message has been transmitted to its high
                    destination.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Bacon.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
